# Docker runs these files on Linux, whatever the host is.
#
# Without an explicit `eol=lf`, a Windows checkout writes CRLF. The kernel then reads the
# shebang as `/bin/bash\r` and the container dies with "no such file or directory" — a
# failure that gives no hint about line endings. Pin LF on every file a container reads.
*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile     text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
.env.example  text eol=lf

# Real portal downloads: UTF-16 LE with CRLF. Any line-ending change corrupts them.
*.csv         binary
